## Collection Toolbar

The bar above a collection: a search box, one row of filter badges with counts, and a right-hand slot for the view switcher and the Add action.

```ts
import { CollectionToolbar } from '@cardstack/catalog/components/collection-toolbar';

<CollectionToolbar
  @search={{this.search}}
  @onSearch={{this.setSearch}}
  @badges={{this.badges}}
  @activeBadge={{this.badge}}
  @onBadge={{this.setBadge}}
>
  <:right>…</:right>
</CollectionToolbar>
```

The toolbar holds no state: the caller owns the search text and the active badge. `'all'` must be the first badge. A collection with more than one filter axis passes them in the `filters` block, which renders inside one Filters dropdown, and `@activeFilterCount` shows how many differ from their defaults.

### Non-goals

It does not query or filter rows itself.
